  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Smaller/newer creators tend to have trouble getting their worlds public. You can end up in CL indefinitely even if your world has a good enough of hype around it to start, but loses its \"heat\" as the VRChat website calls it, all within a matter of days. I understand that CL exists to supposedly speed up the process of getting your world to be Public and searchable as well as keep people from loading into completely broken worlds with absolutely no effort.\nBut this hurts creators who struggle to attract an audience despite having a well-made world. If I'm having problems with this, there's no doubt other small creators have this problem with their hard work, too. I have an idea that can at least improve this system.\nGive Community Labs the ability to be approved (while still being reported if need be) by players, like the upvote system here. Factors such as how frequently non-friends of the creator approve the worlds, whether or not the world creator is present in the instance where an approval/upvote is made can possibly affect it as well. Heat works for a while, but after some time, it'll wear off, usually by being buried by new worlds in the CL section of the Worlds menu.\nPlease consider making these or similar changes to encourage content creators.\nThanks,\nLowPolyBunny",
